//
// Conduit (--use-conduit) end-to-end run for the streaming-mode skip on
// `via_cascade = true` (Track C debt; pairs with lit pin
//   test/Dialect/Conduit/infer_iter_count_skip_for_stream.mlir).
//
// What this proves on real HW:
//   - Pass A's streaming-mode skip on the via_cascade arm produces a
//     conduit.create that downstream Pass C / aie-standard-lowering /
//     peano can chain into a runnable cascade-routed design.
//   - aie.objectfifo {via_cascade = true} composes with the rest of the
//     conduit pipeline well enough to dispatch on real silicon (smallest
//     possible exercise: 1 input vector → cascade hop → 1 output vector).
//
// Why no paired stateful.lit (deliberate deviation from
// conduit_canonicalize_channel_puts/* convention): the upstream stateful
// objectfifo expansion has NO `via_cascade` handler — `grep "viaCascade"
// mlir-aie/lib/` returns only ObjectFifoToConduit.cpp.  Under stateful,
// the attribute is silently ignored and the cascade objectfifo would
// route via DMA, exercising an entirely different physical path; a
// byte-equivalence claim across pipelines would be meaningless.  The
// PASS gate here is internal-consistency: dispatch completes and the
// 16 i32 input bytes round-trip through the cascade port unchanged.
//
// Cascade adjacency tile(0,3) → tile(1,3) (East direction: input=West,
// output=East) is supported on both AIE2 NPU variants — the verifier
// constraint in AIEDialect.cpp::ConfigureCascadeOp::verify only requires
// inputDir ∈ {North, West} and outputDir ∈ {South, East} on AIE2, which
// covers both BaseNPU1TargetModel and BaseNPU2TargetModel (both inherit
// AIE2TargetModel).  cascade_flows/aie.mlir gates on ryzen_ai_npu1 only
// because it predates npu2 hardware; geometry is portable.  Dual RUN-line
// pattern below mirrors test/npu-xrt/shim_dma_bd_reuse/run.lit.
//
// REQUIRES: ryzen_ai, peano
//
// Kernel compute is inline `vector.transfer_read` / `memref.store` /
// `memref.load` / `vector.transfer_write` over `vector<16xi32>` — no
// floating-point conversion, so chess `fp_to_bf16` is NOT the trigger
// here.  Peano routing is selected for consistency with sibling Conduit
// npu-xrt fixtures (`fuse_operators_convergent_npu/conduit.lit`,
// `fuse_core_bodies_npu/conduit.lit`) and with the older Peano-routed
// siblings `loadpdi/run.lit` and `vec_vec_add_objfifo_init/aie2.py`,
// avoiding the chess-toolchain dependency entirely on the conduit pipeline.
//
// RUN: cp %S/aie.mlir aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu1% sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu1_2col/g' -i aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% sed 's/NPUDEVICE/npu2_2col/g' -i aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: %python aiecc.py --no-aiesim --no-xchesscc --no-xbridge --aie-generate-xclbin --aie-generate-npu-insts --no-compile-host --use-conduit --xclbin-name=aie.xclbin --npu-insts-name=insts.bin aie_arch.mlir
// RUN: clang %S/test.cpp -o test.exe -std=c++17 -Wall %xrt_flags -lrt -lstdc++ %test_utils_flags
// RUN: %run_on_npu1% ./test.exe -x aie.xclbin -k MLIR_AIE -i insts.bin
// RUN: %run_on_npu2% ./test.exe -x aie.xclbin -k MLIR_AIE -i insts.bin
